  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 223 PM MDT Fri Sep 11 2026\n\nSunday night into Monday morning shows a cold \nfront passing over the CWA. After this front moves out, a ridge \nstarts to build, bringing cooler temperatures and dryer air. Some \nstorm and shower activity is possible Tuesday evening with return \nflow. A shortwave passes through on Thursday evening, allowing the \nridge to continue to build. On Friday the ridge gets pushed out by a \ntrough forming over the region. Some models are showing \nprecipitation potential Friday afternoon, but more to come on that \nas we get closer. 700mb temperatures are in the 10-15C range in this \nlong term period. Temperatures start to cool off and feel more like \nfall as the week progresses.",
